  "text": "Pip gives Grandma’s story to Mara.\n\nLet Grandma bring out the cushions\n\nThe outer boundaries of something.\n\nWaiting for microphone permission…\n\nThought about something carefully.\n\nThe seed is aboard the small boat.\n\nCarry on with what you were doing.\n\nRina, who is waiting with the loaf\n\nA flat dish used for serving food.\n\nSo ill that she is unable to come.\n\nFasten something by making a knot.\n\nDecide which possibility you want.\n\nA way that two things are related.\n\nThe lantern-flower has taken root.\n\nTouching or pressing on something.\n\nPulled something along the ground.\n\nYou are Pip. Choose your response.\n\nSmall pools of water on a surface.\n\nMade something easier for someone.\n\nA light inside a protective cover.\n\nA thing that is not named exactly.\n\nWords that make something clearer.\n\nPlant it with Grandma before dark.\n\nThe first version, before changes.\n\nMake sure everyone knows the plan.\n\nGave someone information in words.\n\nWeighing more than something else.\n\nDamaged by a split in its surface.\n\nShare stories in Grandma’s garden.\n\nThe baker whose roof Sol repaired.\n\nYour Garden Adventure is complete.\n\nOn some occasions, but not always.\n\nPulling something along a surface.\n\nThink about why the boy hesitated\n\nFind a way for everyone to share.\n\nHelp Rina keep her bread promise.\n\ntranslate(193 24) scale(.413 .48)\n\nDid what he had said he would do.\n\nEvery one, considered separately.\n\nChoose a memory for Pip’s lantern\n\nHand something to another person.\n\nM-31 11q-7-35 4-49h38q16 20 9 49Z\n\nArrange a gathering with Grandma.\n\nStopped something from happening.\n\nRemained in a place or situation.\n\nFall or move to a lower position.\n\nHelp the garden’s stories return.\n\nReread what Grandma and Mara said\n\nYou brought the stories together.\n\nShows a particular place or time.",
